{
  "rule": "A held value of 4 or more Unicode code points is withheld wherever it occurs, as a substring. A shorter value is withheld only as a whole token: where the code point right before it and the one right after it are each not in Unicode general category L* (letters) or Nd (decimal digits), or are the start or end of the text; so No and Nl characters such as '²', '½' and 'Ⅵ' are boundaries (Python: not str.isalnum). Values are tried longest first by code-point count, ties in the order given, in one pass over the original text: an occurrence overlapping one already chosen, or a [withheld] marker already in the text, is skipped. Each occurrence becomes [withheld].",
  "cases": [
